2026-09-27T04:47:56.9153567Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9153669Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9153833Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9153972Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154020Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154123Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154184Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154260Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154440Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154545Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154603Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154740Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9154984Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9155090Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9155324Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9155502Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9155824Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9156071Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9156130Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9156348Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9206737Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9206967Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9207431Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9207751Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9207821Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9208004Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9208095Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9209181Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9210128Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9210318Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9210662Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9211002Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9211423Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9211846Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9212250Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9212452Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9212935Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9213125Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9213241Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9214075Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9215437Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9215966Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9216678Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:56.9216857Z 
